      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The anesthesist is very often asked to manage severe painful syndromes in patients suffering widespread malignant tumours. So often, the extent of neoplastic diffusion is such that common technics for analgesic block cannot be performed. The chemiolysis of the hypophysis-according to Moricca-performed primarily for therapeutic purposes has also shown a powerful analgesic effect."},
